# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust the values for your machine:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — it holds YOUR local overrides and never gets
# committed. Docker Compose reads it automatically for ${VAR} substitution in
# docker-compose.yml, and the Makefile picks up the four host-port variables
# below so the URLs `make dev-up` / `make prod-up` print match the ports
# actually bound. Shell environment wins over `.env` (like compose itself):
# `FRONTEND_PORT=9999 make dev-up` beats a value in this file.
#
# Format: keep it simple — one `KEY=value` per line, `#` for comments. No
# quotes needed for plain values (ports, bare paths). Never put secrets here
# that you would not want on disk in the working tree.
#
# If a variable is missing from `.env`, docker-compose.yml falls back to its
# documented default (see the `${VAR:-default}` expressions in the compose
# file) — so this file is entirely optional. The defaults below use a +10000
# offset from the built-in defaults to avoid clashing with sibling projects
# (every other Vite project wants 5173, several Postgres run on 5432, etc.).
#
# Not overridable here by design: HOST_UID / HOST_GID (the Makefile passes the
# current user's id/gid to compose) and HOME (the sandbox always uses
# /home/devuser; HOST_HOME below controls which host configs get mounted).

# --- Host ports (only these touch your machine; container-side stays fixed) ---

# Vite dev server (development stack). Built-in fallback: 5173.
FRONTEND_PORT=15173

# Dev API via air (development stack). Built-in fallback: 8081.
HOST_PORT=18081

# Production API (production stack). Built-in fallback: 8080.
API_PORT=18080

# Host port for the shared dev/prod Postgres. Built-in fallback: 5432.
POSTGRES_PORT=15432

# --- Optional ---

# Host home directory mounted read-only into the dev sandbox (configs for gh,
# opencode, gitconfig, and the opencode binary). Defaults to $HOME.
# HOST_HOME=/home/your-user

# GitHub tokens forwarded into the dev sandbox (either name works; the dev
# sandbox validates whichever is set). Not read from this file by the
# Makefile's token resolver — export them in your shell instead, or leave
# empty/commented to fall back to the gh credential store.
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Compose project name. It prefixes every resource the stack creates
# (containers such as "<name>-db-1", the default network "<name>_default",
# the "<name>_pgdata" volume), so a SECOND checkout of this repo on the same
# machine must set its own value here or it collides with the first (container
# name conflicts, shared database volume). Defaults to: distributed-task-queue.
# PROJECT_NAME=my-other-copy

# Local dev image tag shared by the `dev` and `frontend` services. Give a
# second checkout its own tag so concurrent `make dev-up` runs do not race on
# one image. Defaults to: distributed-task-queue-dev.
# DEV_IMAGE=my-other-copy-dev